  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 102.70 Expedited permit (EXP)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 102.70 “Expedited permit (EXP)” means an authorization to proceed with work in a jurisdictional area that is conferred by the department and that is not a standard permit or a lower scrutiny approval.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945, (formerly Env-Wt 102.71)",
